  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Peperomin B exerts its biological activity through multiple pathways, ultimately targeting SNU-387. The primary target of Peperomin B is Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is involved in regulating cellular signaling processes. This enzyme is also a target of other compounds, including sec-Butyl acetate, (-)-, and Quercetin 3-(6''-p-hydroxybenzoylgalactoside), all of which have been shown to interact with SNU-387. The final scores from the evidence suggest that Peperomin B's interaction with SNU-387 is supported by multiple indirect pathways, indicating a complex network of molecular interactions. The evidence highlights the role of protein phosphatases in mediating the effects of these compounds, but the exact mechanism by which Peperomin B directly influences SNU-387 remains partially understood. The integration of these findings suggests that Peperomin B may act through a series of downstream targets, with SNU-387 being a downstream effector in the signaling cascade."
